# {{.Tool}} CLI

## When To Use This Skill

Use this skill when operating the `{{.Tool}}` CLI from this repository through command help, stable JSON, non-interactive automation, or dry-run previews.

## Discover The CLI

Inspect `{{.Tool}} --help` and the rungrad manifest with `{{.Tool}} __rungrad_manifest` before planning unfamiliar commands. Use command help for a specific command before adding unfamiliar flags or arguments.

## Safe Command Policy

Prefer `--json` for read commands and parseable command results. Use `--no-prompt` in automation.

Run `--dry-run` before any mutating command that supports it. Treat `{{.Tool}} update --check` as the read-only update check generated by the scaffold.

Require explicit user intent before destructive commands. Use `--confirm` only for generated commands that document that confirmation pattern.

Avoid printing, logging, or requesting secrets in chat.

